import ../../site/editor/entry.dl
import site_fixture.dl

set instance to an instance of website fixture
set view to a new UI view
set view's instance to the address of instance
set state to a new website state
set state's services to the browser UI service provider
set state's view to the address of view
set instance's state to (the address of state) as a pointer
prepare website fixture editors in (the address of state)
set editor to the UI source editor labeled "IDE source" in (state's language)
set main to editor's document's project's entry
set provided to a JSON object containing [JSON text "provided.dl" is "a project helper means: 7"]
configure UI source document main named (main's filename) at (main's uri) prefixed by (main's prefix) using (a copy of JSON-RPC node (main's project's profiles)) with files provided
free provided
set source to the string form of "import lib/std.dl\nprint line \"linked é😀\""
set query to a JSON object containing [JSON text "code64" is (the Base64 URL form of source), JSON text "name" is "linked.dl", JSON text "autorun" is "1"]
apply website editor entry query in (the address of state)
require condition (main's project's files has JSON member named "provided.dl") reporting "Loading a renamed source discarded its provided project files."
require condition ((the UI value for (the control labeled "IDE source" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance))'s text = source) reporting "The shared source link lost Unicode text"
require condition ((the website source filename in (the address of state)) = "linked.dl") reporting "The shared source link lost its filename"
require condition ((the item at 2 in (state's programs))'s phase = 1) reporting "The shared source link did not honor autorun"
set request to state's requests' id
set the text of "IDE source" in (the address of instance) to "edited source"
apply website editor entry query in (the address of state)
require condition (state's requests' id = request) reporting "An unchanged location ran the source twice"
require condition ((the UI value for (the control labeled "IDE source" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance))'s text = "edited source") reporting "An unchanged location discarded source edits"
free query
set editor to the UI source editor labeled "IDE source" in (state's language)
set main to editor's document's project's entry
synchronize UI source workspace (state's language) at 1.0 seconds
set helper to a UI source document named "helper.dl" at "file:///lib/helper.dl" containing "An imported definition" in (main's project)
visit UI source document helper selecting 0 through 1 in editor in (the address of view)
set query to a JSON object containing [JSON text "code" is "plain source", JSON text "name" is "plain.dl"]
apply website editor entry query in (the address of state)
free query
require condition ((the UI value for (the control labeled "IDE source" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance))'s text = "plain source") reporting "A plain shared source link was ignored"
require condition ((editor's document = main) and (editor's locations = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI source location))) reporting "A new source link retained an imported view or the preceding program's navigation history."
set query to a JSON object containing [JSON text "code64" is "Zh", JSON text "code" is "must not load"]
apply website editor entry query in (the address of state)
free query
require condition ((the UI value for (the control labeled "IDE source" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance))'s text = "plain source") reporting "An invalid encoding silently selected another source"
set query to a JSON object containing [JSON text "code" is "must not load", JSON text "name" is "../outside.dl"]
apply website editor entry query in (the address of state)
free query
require condition ((the website source filename in (the address of state)) = "plain.dl") reporting "A source link accepted directory traversal"
set query to a JSON object containing [JSON text "mode" is "unknown", JSON text "code" is "must not load"]
apply website editor entry query in (the address of state)
free query
require condition ((the website editor uses shaders in (the address of state)) = false) reporting "An invalid editor mode changed the selected tab"
set query to a JSON object containing [JSON text "mode" is "shader", JSON text "scene" is "unknown"]
apply website editor entry query in (the address of state)
free query
require condition (state's shader editor's source request = 0) reporting "An unknown scene initiated a source load"
set query to a JSON object containing [JSON text "mode" is "shader", JSON text "scene" is "endless-terrain"]
apply website editor entry query in (the address of state)
free query
require condition (the website editor uses shaders in (the address of state)) reporting "A shader scene link did not select its editor"
require condition (state's shader editor's description's geometry's kind = 1) reporting "A scene link lost its terrain geometry"
require condition (state's shader editor's source request = state's requests' id) reporting "A scene source load has no request owner"
set query to a JSON object containing [JSON text "mode" is "shader", JSON text "scene" is "nano-choreography"]
apply website editor entry query in (the address of state)
free query
require condition (state's shader editor's description's geometry's kind = 2) reporting "Replacing a scene did not replace its geometry"
set query to a JSON object containing [JSON text "mode" is "shader", JSON text "code" is "shader source", JSON text "name" is "preview.dl"]
apply website editor entry query in (the address of state)
free query
require condition (state's shader editor's source request = 0) reporting "An inline shader retained its previous scene fetch"
require condition (state's shader editor's description's geometry's kind = 0) reporting "An inline shader retained its previous scene geometry"
require condition ((the website source filename in (the address of state)) = "preview.dl") reporting "The inline shader lost its filename"
set pending to state's requests
loop while pending != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to website request):
    set next to pending's next
    deallocate pending
    set pending to next
release website fixture editors in (the address of state)
close the address of instance
print line "Shared code links retain Unicode source, filenames, autorun and edits across repeated locations."
